\v 11 Then¦125546 she made a vow¦125547, saying¦125548, “Commander Yahweh¦125549, if¦125551 you \add ≈would only notice the¦125556 misery\add* of your female servant and remember¦125558 me. Don't¦125559 \add ≈ignore\add* \add *me\add*. \add ≈Help\add* your female servant \add ≈to give birth to a son\add*, then¦125546 I'll¦125569 give him¦125569 to \add *you\add* \add ≈for¦125570 his entire¦125571\add* life¦125574, and \add ≈he'll never have his hair cut\add*.”\x + \xo 1:11: \xt Num 6:5.\x*
\p
\v 12 As she¦125585 continued praying to Yahweh¦125588, Eli¦125589 was¦125590 watching¦125590 her¦125593 mouth¦125593.
\v 13 \add ≈Now\add* Hannah was¦125597 \add ≈praying from her heart¦125600\add*, and¦125595 her lips¦125602 were¦125603 moving \add ≈but¦125595 she wasn't speaking¦125597 aloud\add*. Eli¦125608 thought \add she must be\add* drunk¦125609,
\v 14 and¦125611 \add ≈scolded\add* her¦125612, “You¦125622 shouldn't be¦125617 getting drunk¦125617. Get¦125613 rid of¦125621 your¦125621 wine¦125621.”
\p
\v 15 “No¦125627, my master¦125628,” Hannah¦125625 replied¦125624, “I'm a woman¦125629 \add ≈who's suffering deep down\add*. I haven't drunk¦125637 any wine¦125634 or intoxicating drink¦125635, \add ≈but¦125624 rather\add* I've¦125637 been \add ≈sharing my inner issues\add* with Yahweh¦125628.
\v 16 Don't¦125645 think that your¦125650 female servant¦125650 is \add just\add* a worthless¦125654 woman, because¦125655 just now I¦125660 was \add ≈praying as a result of my¦125659 terrible anguish¦125658 and¦125659 frustration\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “\add Then\add* go¦125668 in peace¦125669,” Eli¦125666 replied. “And may Yisrael's¦125671 god¦125670 grant¦125672 your¦125675 request that¦125676 you¦125677 \add ≈presented to\add* him¦125678.”
\p
\v 18 “\add ≈Please assume the best of\add* your female servant¦125682,” said¦125680 \add @Hannah\add*, then¦125680 she¦125681 went¦125685 on¦125684 her way¦125687 and \add ≈had something to eat¦125688\add*, and \add ≈something had changed in¦125684 her demeanor\add*.
\s1 Shemu'el's birth and dedication
\rem /s1 Samuel's Birth and Dedication
\p
\v 19 They \add all\add* gut up early¦125697 the¦125700 \add next\add* morning¦125698 and worshipped¦125699 Yahweh \add again\add*, then¦125697 they¦125703 returned¦125702 to their¦125706 home at¦125698 Ramah¦125707. Then¦125697 Elkanah¦125709 \add ≈slept with¦125698\add* his¦125713 wife¦125713 Hannah¦125712, and Yahweh \add ≈answered her¦125714 prayer\add*.
\v 20 \add @Hannah¦125721\add* got pregnant¦125720, and¦125717 in due course, she gave¦125722 birth¦125722 to a son¦125723. She named¦125724 him ‘Shemu'el’ \add (meaning ‘heard by God’, usually changed to ‘Samuel’ in English)\add* because¦125729 she had requested him from Yahweh¦125730.
