\p
\v 21 \add At the usual time,\add* Elkanah¦125735 and all¦125736 his¦125738 household¦125738 went \add to Shiloh\add* to \add ≈offer¦125739 their sacrifices¦125743 and fulfill their vows\add* to Yahweh¦125740.
\v 22 \add ≈But¦125749\add* Hannah \add ≈didn't¦125750 accompany them\add* because¦125752 she'd told her¦125755 husband¦125755, “I'll¦125759 \add come and\add* bring¦125759 him¦125759 when he's weaned¦125757. Then¦125749 he can be \add ≈taken¦125759 in to\add* Yahweh¦125764 and \add ≈permanently\add* remain¦125765 there¦125766.”
\v 23 “Do \add ≈what you think's best\add*,” her husband¦125774 \add ≈replied\add*. “Stay until you've weaned him. May¦125784 Yahweh¦125785 \add ≈do¦125775 whatever he¦125784 said¦125771\add* \add to you\add*.” \add ≈So¦125771\add* \add *she\add* stayed \add behind\add* and¦125771 breastfed her son¦125794 until she \add ≈eventually\add* weaned him.
\p
\v 24 \add The next year,\add* after she'd weaned¦125803 him, she took¦125800 the young¦125804 boy with \add #them\add*, along with three¦125805 bulls¦125804, a \add ≈sack\add* of flour¦125808, and¦125800 a \add ≈container\add* of wine¦125810. Then¦125800 she brought¦125811 him to Yahweh's¦125814 \add ≈tent\add* in¦125804 Shiloh¦125815,
\v 25 and¦125823 after slaughtering¦125819 the bull¦125822, they¦125823 took the boy¦125826 in to¦125827 Eli¦125829.
\v 26 “Please, my master,” \add @Hannah\add* said¦125831. “As your spirit lives, my master, I'm the¦125838 woman¦125838 who¦125839 was standing¦125839 with¦125841 you¦125840 here to pray¦125842 to Yahweh¦125833.
\v 27 I prayed¦125851 \add ≈that¦125858 Yahweh¦125853 would give¦125852 me a son, and he¦125852 did, and this is him¦125860\add*.
\v 28 Also¦125862, I dedicated him¦125864 to Yahweh all¦125866 his life, so he's now given to Yahweh.”
\p Then¦125862 \add #they\add* worshipped¦125874 Yahweh there¦125875.
