\p
\v 18 \add ≈By now\add* Shemuel was¦126164 serving¦126164 Yahweh¦126168, dressed in a priestly uniform made from linen¦126172.
\v 19 \add ≈Each¦126190 year\add* his mother¦126179 would make¦126176 a small¦126175 robe¦126174 for him and¦126174 bring¦126180 it when¦126185 she¦126185 came with¦126185 her¦126188 husband¦126188 to¦126189 offer¦126189 \add #their sacrifices¦126192\add*.
\v 20 Eli¦126196 would bless¦126195 Elkanah¦126199 and his¦126202 wife¦126202 and say, “May¦126204 Yahweh \add ≈give more children for¦126206 you through\add* this¦126211 woman¦126210 in¦126212 place¦126212 of¦126212 the¦126213 \add boy\add* \add ≈dedicated\add* to Yahweh.” Then¦126195 they'd return home¦126218.
\p
\v 21 \add ≈So\add* Yahweh visited¦126222 Hannah¦126226 and she went on to give¦126228 birth¦126228 to three¦126229 \add other\add* sons¦126231 and two¦126232 daughters¦126233. \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* \add ≈young\add* Shemuel¦126236 \add ≈grew¦126234 up¦126234 serving\add* Yahweh.
