\p
\v 22 \add ≈Now\add* Eli¦126242 was¦126243 very old¦126243 and he¦126245 had heard¦126245 all¦126247 about what his¦126251 sons¦126251 were doing¦126250 to¦126252 the Israeli people, and \add also\add* that they¦126258 were sleeping around with¦126259 the women¦126261 who¦126262 worked at the sacred¦126264 tent¦126264 entrance.
\v 23 “Why are¦126270 you¦126270 \add two\add* doing¦126270 all these things that I keep hearing¦126275 about—these evil things \add ≈affecting\add* all those people¦126283?” he \add ≈asked\add* them.
\v 24 “No, my sons¦126287. The reports¦126292 that¦126293 I keep hearing¦126295 Yahweh's¦126299 people¦126297 passing on aren't¦126289 good¦126291!
\v 25 If someone sins against a person, then God¦126307 will mediate¦126306 for him¦126306, but¦126306 if¦126308 someone sins against Yahweh, who will \add ≈speak up\add* for that person?” \add ≈But¦126306\add* they¦126318 wouldn't listen¦126318 to their¦126320 father's¦126320 advice because¦126321 Yahweh wanted to put¦126325 them¦126325 to death¦126325.
\p
\v 26 \add ≈Meanwhile\add* the boy¦126327 Shemuel was growing¦126330 \add up\add*, and his good¦126331 \add behaviour pleased\add* both¦126332 Yahweh¦126335 and \add ≈the people¦126339\add*.\x + \xo 2:26: \xt Luk 2:52.\x*
\s1 The prophecy against Eli's family
