\p
\v 27 \add ≈One day\add* one of¦126343 God's¦126345 \add prophets\add* came¦126342 to Eli¦126348 and¦126349 told him¦126350, “This is what Yahweh¦126353 says¦126352, ‘Did\add n't\add* I clearly reveal myself¦126355 to your ancestors¦126359 when they were Far'oh's \add ≈slaves\add* in¦126361 Egypt¦126361?
\v 28 And out of all the Israeli¦126369 tribes¦126369, I chose¦126365 \add @your ancestor¦126384\add* to be a priest¦126372 to me, to go¦126373 up¦126373 on¦126374 my¦126381 altar¦126376, to burn¦126377 incense¦126378, \add and\add* to \add ≈wear the sacred apron in front of me\add*. Plus I gave¦126382 your ancestors¦126384 \add the rights to\add* all the burnt offerings¦126389 made¦126377 by the \add ≈Israelis¦126370\add*.\x + \xo 2:28: a \xt Exo 28:1-4; \xo b \xt Lev 7:35-36.\x*
\v 29 Why do you \add ≈disrespect\add* sacrifices¦126395 and¦126396 offerings¦126396 that¦126397 I commanded¦126398 \add the people\add* to bring to me \add ≈at¦126395 my residence\add*. And¦126400 \add ≡why do\add* you honour¦126400 your¦126403 sons¦126403 more¦126404 than¦126404 me by¦126405 fattening yourselves¦126405 from¦126406 the best of every¦126407 offering¦126409 of my people Yisrael¦126410?’
\p
\v 30 “Therefore, this is what Yahweh¦126416 the god¦126417 of Yisrael¦126418 declares: ‘I indeed¦126419 said¦126420 \add ≈your ancestors¦126423 and then your descendants\add* would \add ≈serve me forever¦126428\add*.’ But¦126422 now \add ≈I declare this\add* \add instead\add*: ‘\add ≈This cannot continue\add* because¦126435 I will honour those who honour me, but¦126422 those who despise¦126439 me will be¦126440 \add ≈side-lined\add*.
\v 31 Listen¦126445, the time¦126443 is coming¦126444 when I'll¦126453 \add ≈bring you and¦126445 your relatives to an¦126455 end—none of your men will die of old¦126455 age\add*
\v 32 and¦126468 you'll see¦126458 distress¦126459 in my residence. I'll¦126465 do¦126464 good¦126464 for \add the rest of\add* Yisrael¦126467, but¦126458 there'll never be¦126470 another old¦126471 man¦126471 in your¦126472 home.
\v 33 I¦126480 won't¦126478 \add ≈finish\add* them off¦126480 near my¦126483 altar¦126483. Your¦126487 eyes¦126487 will fail¦126484 and¦126477 you'll grieve¦126488 \add ≈inside\add*, but¦126477 your¦126491 \add adult sons\add* will die¦126496.
\v 34 This¦126499 will be¦126502 the sign¦126502: it'll \add ≈turn out\add* that¦126503 your¦126508 two¦126507 sons¦126508 Hofni¦126511 and¦126512 Finehas¦126512 will both¦126507 die¦126515 on the same day¦126513.\x + \xo 2:34: \xt 1Sam 4:11.\x*
\v 35 Then¦126518 I'll \add ≈select\add* another man to be a faithful priest¦126520 to me—he'll \add ≈follow my desires and do what's in¦126523 my mind¦126523\add*. I'll make \add ≈him and his faithful descendants to continue and to always serve me\add*.
\v 36 Any of¦126540 your¦126543 descendants who¦126542 remain¦126542 \add ≈alive\add* will¦126544 have to go to him¦126546 to request food¦126551 and money and \add ≈beg\add* for some priestly¦126558 work to earn \add ≈something to eat¦126559\add*.’ ”
\c 3
\s1 Yahweh calls Shemuel
\rem /s1 The Lord Appears to Samuel; Samuel's Calling and Prophetic Activity; The Lord Speaks to Samuel; The Lord Calls Samuel
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Meanwhile young\add* Shemuel was serving¦126567 Yahweh \add ≈under\add* Eli¦126572. In those¦126579 days¦126578, Yahweh rarely \add ≈spoke to the people or sent visions¦126581\add*.
\p
\v 2 \add ≈By that time,\add* Eli's¦126588 \add ≈sight was very poor\add*—he could barely see¦126598. \add One night when\add* he was sleeping in his place,\f + \fr 3:2 \ft Some translations use ‘room’ here instead of ‘place’, but it could easily be that he had a small bed in a corner somewhere.\f*
\v 3 and¦126604 Shemuel¦126604 was lying¦126605 down in¦126606 Yahweh's¦126607 tent (where¦126608 the box¦126611 was that contained the \add ≈stone slabs\add*), \add ≈but¦126600\add* God's¦126612 lamp¦126600 was still burning.
\v 4 Yahweh¦126616 called out to¦126617 Shemuel¦126619, and¦126620 he¦126620 \add ≈called back\add*, “I'm here¦126621. \add Coming.\add*”
\v 5 Then¦126623 he¦126623 ran¦126623 to¦126624 Eli¦126626 and¦126627 said¦126627, “Here¦126628 I am¦126628, because¦126629 you¦126631 called me¦126632.”
\p “I didn't¦126634 call,” he said. “Go back \add and\add* lie¦126638 down.” \add ≈So¦126623\add* he went¦126639 \add back\add* and laid¦126640 down.
\p
\v 6 Yahweh¦126644 called again¦126646, “Shemuel¦126647.”
\p Shemuel got up¦126648 and went¦126650 to¦126651 Eli¦126653 and said¦126654, “Here¦126655 I am¦126655, because¦126656 you¦126657 called me¦126658.”
\p “I didn't¦126660 call¦126645, my son,” he¦126643 said, “Go back \add and\add* lie¦126665 down¦126665.”
\p
\v 7 (\add At this point\add*, Shemuel didn't¦126668 \add really\add* know¦126669 Yahweh, because Yahweh hadn't revealed¦126674 \add himself\add* to¦126675 him¦126675 before.)
\v 8 Then Yahweh called Shemuel a third¦126685 time¦126685. He got up¦126686 and went¦126687 to¦126688 Eli¦126690 and said¦126691, “Here¦126692 I am¦126692, because¦126693 you¦126694 called me¦126695.”
\p Then Eli realised that¦126698 it was Yahweh who was calling the boy¦126701
\v 9 and he told Shemuel, “Go¦126706 \add and\add* lie¦126707 down. Then¦126703 if¦126709 he calls¦126711 to¦126712 you \add again\add*, \add ≈just answer\add*, ‘Speak¦126714, Yahweh¦126715, because¦126716 your¦126718 servant¦126718 is¦126717 listening¦126717.’ ” \add ≈So¦126703\add* Shemuel went¦126719 and laid¦126721 down \add again\add* in¦126722 his¦126722 place¦126722.
\p
