\p \add At that time,\add* Yisrael went to war against the Philistines. They¦126960 camped at Eben-Ezer, and the Philistines camped at Afek¦126967.
\v 2 Then¦126969 the Philistines lined up to¦126971 meet¦126971 Yisrael and the battle spread¦126973. Yisrael was¦126975 defeated¦126975 by the Philistines and they¦126979 killed¦126979 about¦126982 4,000 warriors in the battle line¦126980 in the countryside¦126981.
\v 3 \add ≈As\add* the people\f + \fr 4:3 \ft It seems that most translations assume that this is referring to the remainder of the warriors staggering back into the camp (which is certainly a possibility), but we've interpreted it as the people coming together (with their elders as it says), to try to figure out why they were defeated. (Similarly for v4.)\f* came¦126986 into the camp, the \add ≈Israeli¦126992\add* elders \add ≈asked\add* \add themselves\add*, “Why did Yahweh \add ≈allow the Philistines¦126999 to slaughter\add* us today? Let's get the box¦127005 from Shiloh¦127002 that contains \add the stone slabs with\add* Yahweh's¦126996 agreement¦127006 \add on them\add*. \add ≈Once it's amongst us\add*, \add surely\add* it'll save¦127010 us from \add ≈defeat¦126995 by\add* our¦127012 enemies¦127012.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦127014\add* the people¦127015 sent¦127014 \add <men\add* to Shiloh¦127016 and from¦127018 there they¦127017 lifted the box containing Yahweh's¦127023 agreement \add and the sacred platform\add* with the winged creatures.\f + \fr 4:4 \ft And with Commander Yahweh sitting on, above, or between them.\f* Eli's¦127031 two¦127028 sons¦127029, Hofni¦127037 and Finehas, were there with the box containing God's agreement.\x + \xo 4:4: \xt Exo 25:22.\x*
\p
\v 5 \add ≈As¦127052\add* the box¦127042 with Yahweh's¦127045 agreement¦127043 \add ≈was carried\add* into¦127046 the camp¦127048, all¦127050 the \add ≈Israelis¦127050\add* shouted¦127053 so loud that the ground shook¦127055.
\v 6 When¦127058 the Philistines¦127059 heard¦127058 the \add ≈noise\add*, they said¦127064, “What's¦127065 that loud shout¦127067 in¦127070 the Hebrews' camp?” Then¦127058 they realised that the box¦127074 \add ≈with¦127070 Yahweh's¦127075 covenant\add* had¦127076 come¦127076 into¦127077 their camp
\v 7 and¦127081 they were afraid saying, “A god¦127086 has¦127085 come¦127085 into¦127087 the \add Israeli\add* camp¦127089.” Then¦127081 they said¦127090, “\add ≈This means trouble\add*, because¦127083 it¦127095 wasn't like¦127096 this¦127096 yesterday¦127097 \add ≈or the previous days¦127098\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈Oh dear\add*! Who¦127102 will¦127103 rescue¦127103 us¦127103 from¦127104 these mighty¦127106 gods? Those are the gods who struck¦127111 the Egyptians with¦127118 every plague¦127117 in¦127118 the wilderness¦127118.
\v 9 Now we Philistines¦127123 \add ≈really need to fight with passion\add*, because if we don't, we'll ending up serving the Hebrews¦127126 just¦127127 like they've had¦127128 to serve¦127125 us. \add ≈Now, gather your courage and fight for your lives\add*.”
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦127134\add* the¦127135 Philistines¦127135 fought¦127134 \add hard\add*, and Yisrael was \add ≈defeated¦127136\add*. \add ≈Many warriors fled¦127138 back to¦127140 their tents¦127140\add* and it¦127141 was a \add ≈terrible\add* slaughter¦127142—30,000 foot¦127149 soldiers¦127149 from Yisrael were killed.
\v 11 \add ≈As well as that,\add* the¦127151 box¦127151 with God's¦127152 \add agreement\add* was¦127153 taken¦127153, and Eli's¦127157 two¦127154 sons¦127155 Hofni¦127159 and Finehas were killed.
\s1 The death of Eli
