\p
\v 12 A Benyamite man¦127163 ran¦127162 from¦127166 the battle¦127166 line¦127166 back to Shiloh¦127168 that¦127170 day¦127169. His¦127171 clothes¦127171 were¦127172 torn¦127172 and¦127162 \add ≈he was¦127174 covered in¦127169 dirt\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈When¦127178\add* he arrived¦127178 \add there\add*, Eli¦127180 was sitting¦127181 on¦127200 a roadside seat¦127184 watching¦127188, because¦127189 he was \add ≈very concerned\add* about the \add ≈sacred chest¦127195\add*. As¦127196 the man¦127197 entered the city¦127200 with¦127200 the news, all¦127202 the \add ≈people\add* started \add ≈wailing loudly\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈As\add* Eli heard the wailing, he¦127212 \add ≈asked\add*, “\add ≈What's¦127213 that¦127216 big commotion¦127215\add*?” \add ≈So¦127206\add* the man¦127217 ran over to Eli to \add ≈tell¦127220 him the news\add*.
