\v 5 (\add ≈Because of that¦127478\add*, until¦127476 this day¦127477 Dagon's priests¦127463 and¦127465 everyone who¦127467 enters Dagon's temple in¦127475 Ashdod¦127475 won't¦127460 tread¦127462 on¦127475 the threshhold¦127473.)
\s1 God punishes the Philistine cities
\p
\v 6 Yahweh¦127484 \add ≈caused a lot of trouble\add* for the \add people of\add* Ashdod¦127487 and he¦127488 terrified¦127488 them. He¦127496 \add ≈caused\add* them and \add ≈the people in¦127491 the region\add* to \add ≈get lumpy growths on¦127491 their skin\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈When¦127501\add* the¦127502 \add ≈leaders\add* in Ashdod¦127504 \add ≈saw¦127501 what was happening\add*, they said¦127508, “The god¦127513 of Yisrael's¦127514 box¦127512 mustn't stay with¦127515 us because¦127505 \add ≈he's punishing\add* \add both\add* us and¦127501 our¦127523 god Dagon¦127522.”
\v 8 \add ≈So\add* they sent¦127525 for all¦127529 the Philistine rulers¦127531, and¦127525 \add when they'd assembled\add* they \add ≈asked\add*, “What¦127535 should¦127543 we¦127537 do¦127537 with the god¦127539 of Yisrael's¦127540 box¦127544?”
\p “Let the god of Yisrael's box be taken around to Gat¦127542,” they \add ≈decided\add*. \add ≈So\add* they moved¦127547 \add *it¦127543\add* \add there\add*.
\v 9 After¦127556 \add ≈it arrived\add*, Yahweh¦127563 \add ≈started punishing Gat\add* and \add both\add* young¦127574 and old men¦127572 in¦127565 the city started getting growths on¦127565 their skin, and it caused a huge¦127567 panic¦127566.
\v 10 \add ≈So¦127583\add* they¦127597 sent¦127583 God's box to Ekron¦127588, \add ≈but¦127583\add* as soon as \add *it\add* entered \add *the city\add*, the Ekronites cried¦127594 out¦127594, “\add Hey!\add* They've brought¦127597 the god¦127602 of Yisrael's¦127603 box here to \add ≈kill¦127604 us\add* and¦127583 our¦127607 people¦127607.”
\v 11 \add ≈So¦127609\add* they sent¦127609 for the Philistine rulers¦127615, and \add ≈when they'd assembled\add* they said¦127617, “Send the god¦127622 of Yisrael's¦127623 box¦127621 away. \add ≈Send it back\add* to its¦127625 place¦127625 \add ≈so\add* it won't¦127626 \add ≈cause us and our people¦127632 to die\add*.” Because¦127633 there was a \add ≈deadly panic¦127636 all¦127639 over\add* the city¦127641 \add as\add* \add ≈God's¦127622 punishment there was severe\add*
\v 12 and¦127657 the men¦127648 who¦127649 didn't¦127650 die¦127652 suffered with¦127654 the growths. \add ≈So¦127648\add* the \add ≈people's\add* cry¦127658 went¦127657 up to the heavens¦127660.
\c 6
\s1 Sending the chest back to Yisrael
