\p
\v 1 \add ≈So¦127662 it¦127662 was that\add* Yahweh's¦127665 box¦127663 was \add held\add* in¦127666 Philistine¦127667 territory¦127666 for seven¦127668 months¦127669,
\v 2 then¦127671 the¦127672 Philistines¦127672 called¦127671 \add &their\add* priests¦127673 and diviners¦127674 and \add ≈asked\add*, “What¦127676 should we do¦127678 with¦127682 Yahweh's¦127680 box¦127679? \add ≈Show us¦127681 how¦127682 we can get it¦127683 back\add* away to¦127684 its¦127684 place¦127684.”
\p
\v 3 “If¦127687 you're going to send the god¦127693 of Yisrael's¦127694 box¦127692 back,” they¦127686 \add ≈responded¦127686\add*, “don't¦127695 send it \add ≈back by itself\add*, but¦127686 definitely return it to him¦127704 with a guilt¦127705 offering¦127705. Then¦127686 you'll all be healed¦127707, and¦127686 you'll all \add ≈understand why you've been suffering\add*.”
\p
\v 4 “What guilt¦127719 offering¦127719 should we¦127721 \add ≈send¦127721 with it\add*?” they \add ≈asked\add*.
\p “Five¦127727 gold \add replicas of the\add* tumours, and five¦127731 gold mice,” they said. “That's the number¦127724 of \add *our\add* rulers¦127739, because¦127734 \add ≈the same\add* plague¦127736 \add ≈affected both them¦127738 and the people\add*.
\v 5 Make¦127741 replicas of the tumours and replicas of the mice¦127746 that have been destroying the land, and it will honour¦127754 Yisrael's¦127753 god¦127752. Then¦127741 perhaps¦127755 he¦127756 will \add ≈less his¦127759 punishment that's been\add* on you and on your gods¦127762 and on your land.
\v 6 Why \add ≈have you¦127767 all been so stubborn\add* just like the Egyptians when Pharaoh¦127774 made \add ≈them stubborn\add*? When¦127766 \add @Yisrael's god\add* dealt¦127780 severely with them, didn't¦127778 \add @the Egyptians\add* send¦127782 \add @the Israelis\add* away¦127782 and¦127766 they¦127772 went¦127783?
\v 7 \add ≈So¦127785\add* now¦127785, \add ≈get a brand\add* new cart with¦127804 two¦127791 nursing¦127793 cows \add ≈which¦127794 have never had a yoke¦127799 on¦127804 their necks\add*. Hitch¦127801 the cows to the cart \add ≈but¦127785\add* take¦127805 their calves¦127806 \add ≈back to their pen\add*.
\v 8 Then¦127810 pick up Yahweh's¦127814 box and put it into¦127817 the cart \add ≈along with\add* the gold¦127823 objects that¦127824 you are \add ≈sending with it\add* as a guilt¦127827 offering¦127827 \add ≈put in¦127829 another container beside the box\add*. \add ≈Finally\add*, send¦127831 \add @the cart\add* away¦127831 and \add off\add* it will¦127833 go¦127833.
\v 9 Then¦127835 watch¦127835 \add <it\add*. If¦127836 it \add ≈heads towards\add* Beyt-Shemesh¦127842 \add ≈in¦127859 Israeli territory¦127839, then it's their god that caused this¦127850 terrible calamity\add*. \add ≈But¦127835\add* if¦127851 not¦127853, then we'll know¦127854 that \add ≈it wasn't the Israeli god, and¦127835 that\add* it \add all\add* happened¦127862 to¦127863 us¦127863 by chance¦127860.”
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦127874 they followed those instructions\add*: they took¦127868 two¦127869 cows¦127870 \add ≈that had been feeding calves\add* and¦127865 hitched¦127872 them¦127872 to the \add new\add* cart¦127873, but¦127865 they shut¦127877 their¦127876 calves away in¦127873 the \add ≈stall\add*.
\v 11 Then¦127880 they¦127880 put¦127880 Yahweh's¦127884 box¦127883 into¦127885 the cart¦127887 with the \add other\add* container with the gold¦127892 mice¦127891 and¦127880 the replicas of their¦127895 tumours¦127895.
\v 12 \add Amazingly,\add* the cows¦127899 went¦127908 straight¦127897 down the road¦127903 going to Beyt-Shemesh. They \add ≈stayed on¦127900 that\add* one highway¦127906, walking and mooing, and they \add ≈never once deviated to the left¦127915 or the right¦127914\add*, and the Philistine rulers¦127916 followed them¦127919 as far as the border¦127922 of¦127922 Beyt-Shemesh.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈Meanwhile in\add* Beyt-Shemesh, \add the people\add* were harvesting¦127928 wheat¦127931 in the valley¦127932, and when they \add ≈looked up¦127933\add* and saw¦127937 the box¦127940, \add ≈they were very happy\add*.
\v 14 The¦127944 cart came¦127945 into the field¦127948 belonging to Yehoshua and \add then the cows just\add* stood there. There was a large¦127957 stone¦127956 there, and \add @the people\add* split¦127958 \add the sides of\add* the wooden cart \add into pieces to start a fire\add*, then offered¦127966 the cows as a burnt¦127967 sacrifice to Yahweh¦127968.
\v 15 Then the Levites¦127971 lifted down¦127972 Yahweh's¦127977 box¦127976 and the \add other\add* container that was with it with the gold¦127989 objects in¦127986 it, and they¦127990 placed them¦127990 on the large¦127994 stone¦127993. Then the men of¦127995 Beyt-Shemesh¦127998 offered¦127999 up¦127999 \add more\add* burnt¦128000 offerings¦128000 and sacrificed¦128002 sacrifices¦128002 to Yahweh on that day¦128003.
\v 16 The five¦128007 Philistine rulers¦128008 watched \add all this from a distance before\add* returning¦128012 to Ekron¦128013 that¦128015 same day¦128014.
\s1 The gold replicas
