\p
\v 19 \add ≈But\add* some Beyt-Shemesh¦128076 men looked¦128078 into Yahweh's¦128080 box¦128079, and¦128072 he¦128072 killed seventy¦128083\f + \fr 6:19 \ft TC: The oldest Hebrew text has 50,070 men being killed here, making it hard to imagine how that many men kept clambering over dead bodies to look into the sacred chest. (But possibly we're not understanding the situation correctly?) We have followed later manuscripts here.\f* of¦128073 them. The people mourned¦128088 because¦128077 Yahweh had¦128078 \add ≈caused such devastation\add* among¦128082 the people.
\s1 The sacred chest is taken to Kiryat-Yearim
