\p
\v 2 The \add ≈sacred chest¦128170 ended up\add* staying in¦128171 Kiriat-Yearim for twenty¦128176 years \add ≈but¦128167 the Israelis¦128182 longed sadly\add* for Yahweh¦128184.
\rem /s1 Samuel Leads Israel to Victory; Samuel as Judge
\p
\v 3 Then Shemuel told all the \add ≈Israelis¦128194\add*, “If¦128196 you all \add really want\add* to return to Yahweh, remove¦128206 the foreign¦128210 gods¦128209 and the Ashtorets¦128212 from \add ≈among¦128211 you\add*. Then \add ≈decide firmly to serve¦128218\add* Yahweh and \add ≈no other\add*, then he'll rescue¦128220 you from the Philistines' \add ≈oppression\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦128225 the Israelis¦128227\add* removed¦128225 the Baal¦128230 and Ashtoret¦128233 \add idols\add*, and \add began to\add* serve¦128234 Yahweh¦128237 only.
\p
\v 5 Then Shemuel¦128242 \add ≈called\add*, “Gather¦128243 all Yisrael¦128248 to Mitspah, and¦128241 I'll pray¦128250 to Yahweh¦128254 for you¦128251 all.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦128256\add* they gathered¦128256 at Mitspah, and drew¦128258 water¦128260 and poured¦128261 it out¦128261 \add ≈in¦128278 front¦128263\add* of Yahweh, and they fasted¦128265 on¦128278 that¦128267 day¦128266 and said¦128268 there¦128269, “We¦128270 have¦128270 sinned¦128270 against Yahweh.” And¦128272 Shemuel¦128273 \add ≈guided\add* the¦128276 \add ≈Israelis¦128277\add* at Mitspah.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈When\add* the Philistines heard that the \add ≈Israelis\add* had¦128284 gathered¦128284 at Mitspah, the Philistine rulers¦128290 \add ≈decided to attack\add* Yisrael¦128287. \add ≈When the Israelis\add* heard \add <that\add*, they¦128299 were afraid of¦128300 the Philistines
