\v 12 Shemuel¦128385 took¦128384 a single rock¦128386 and stood it between¦128389 Mitspah and Shen¦128393. He¦128394 \add ≈named\add* it ‘Eben-Ezer’ \add (which means ‘stone of help’)\add*, saying¦128400, “Yahweh¦128405 helped¦128404 us¦128404 \add ≈all the way up to\add* here.”
\v 13 \add ≈So¦128407\add* the Philistines \add ≈ended up being\add* subdued¦128407 and didn't¦128409 invade¦128413 Yisrael's¦128415 border again¦128412, and Yahweh¦128419 \add ≈worked\add* against the Philistines \add ≈as long as Shemuel lived\add*.
\v 14 The¦128426 cities¦128426 that¦128427 the Philistines had¦128428 taken¦128428 from Ekron¦128435 and as far as Gat¦128438 were returned to Yisrael. And \add so\add* Yisrael rescued their¦128441 territory¦128441 from the Philistines, and there was¦128446 peace¦128447 between¦128448 Yisrael and the Amorites¦128451.
\p
\v 15 \add ≈So¦128453\add* Shemuel¦128454 guided Yisrael¦128457 \add ≈while he¦128453 lived\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈Every year\add* he \add ≈did the circuit¦128466\add* around Beyt-El, Gilgal¦128470, and Mitspah, and he \add ≈helped settled disputes for the people in¦128465\add* all those places¦128479,
