\v 4 \add ≈Eventually,\add* the Israeli¦128542 elders¦128542 met together¦128540 with Shemuel at Ramah¦128548
\v 5 and \add ≈requested\add*, “Listen¦128552, you're old¦128554 \add now\add*, and your sons¦128555 don't¦128556 \add ≈follow your example\add*. \add ≈So¦128550\add* appoint¦128560 a king¦128563 for us now to \add ≈lead\add* us like¦128565 all¦128565 the¦128567 other nations¦128567.”\x + \xo 8:5: \xt Deu 17:14.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈But¦128569\add* Shemuel¦128572 \add ≈thought that their request for a king¦128578 was an evil request, so\add* \add *he¦128580\add* prayed¦128580 to¦128582 Yahweh¦128584
