\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* there was a Benyamite man named Kish¦128846 (son of Abiel¦128849, son of Zeror¦128852, son of Bekorath, son of Afiah¦128858, the son of a Yaminite¦128862 man) \add ≈who was strong and wealthy¦128864\add*.
\v 2 \add @Kish\add* had a son¦128869 \add ≈named\add* Sha'ul¦128871 who was a handsome¦128873 young¦128872 man and good—\add ≈in fact there¦128874 wasn't any Israeli¦128877 man\add* better than him¦128879, \add and\add* he¦128882 was \add ≈head and shoulders¦128880 taller than anyone else\add*.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈One time,\add* the female donkeys of Sha'uls father¦128890 Kish \add ≈had gone missing\add*, and Kish \add ≈told\add* his¦128897 son¦128897, “Take¦128898 one¦128904 of the servants¦128905 with you¦128901, and \add ≈pack up\add* and go¦128907 and find those donkeys.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦128913\add* \add #they\add* passed¦128913 through the Efrayimite hill¦128914 country¦128914, then¦128913 through the Shalishah¦128920 \add ≈region\add*, but they didn't find them. Then¦128913 they went through the Shaalim¦128926 \add ≈region\add*, but there¦128927 was nothing, \add ≈so\add* \add #they\add* \add ≈continued on¦128914\add* through the land¦128929 of¦128929 the Benyamites, but they didn't find them.
\v 5 \add Finally,\add* they¦128936 entered the Tsuf \add ≈area\add*, and \add eventually\add* Sha'ul¦128939 said¦128940 to¦128941 his¦128941 servant¦128941, “Come¦128945 on. Let's¦128946 \add ≈go¦128946 back¦128946 home in case\add* my¦128950 father¦128950 \add ≈stops worrying\add* about the donkeys¦128953 and \add starts\add* worrying about us¦128955.”
