\v 10 “\add ≈Good¦129058 idea\add*,” Sha'ul¦129056 told his¦129057 servant¦129057. “Let's¦129062 go¦129062 then¦129055.” \add ≈So¦129055\add* they¦129063 went¦129063 to¦129064 the city¦129066 there¦129069 where¦129067 the man¦129070 of¦129070 God¦129071 was.
\v 11 They were¦129074 \add ≈climbing up¦129074 the rise towards\add* the city¦129076 \add ≈when\add* they \add ≈met some\add* young¦129079 women¦129079 going¦129074 out¦129080 to¦129081 draw¦129081 water¦129082, and¦129083 they \add ≈asked\add* them¦129084, “Is¦129087 the seer¦129087 in¦129075 \add ≈town¦129076\add*?”
\v 12 “\add ≈Yes¦129093 he is\add*,” they answered¦129089. “Hurry¦129095 \add ≈though\add*, because¦129098 he's come¦129100 to the city¦129101 today \add to offer\add* the sacrifice¦129103 for the people¦129105 at¦129106 the high¦129106 place¦129106.
\v 13 You'll find him as soon as you enter¦129108 the city¦129109, before¦129113 he goes up to the high¦129115 place¦129115 to eat. The people¦129121 won't¦129118 eat until¦129122 he \add ≈gets there\add*, because¦129117 he himself will bless¦129128 the sacrifice¦129129. Afterwards, \add ≈those¦129134 who've been invited¦129134\add* will eat \add together there\add*. So go¦129136 up there now \add ≈and¦129135 you'll soon find him\add*.”
\v 14 \add ≈So¦129144\add* they went¦129144 on up into the city¦129145, and¦129144 as they were¦129147 entering, wow, there was¦129152 Shemuel¦129151 \add ≈coming¦129152 out¦129152 towards¦129153\add* them¦129153 to go¦129154 up to the high¦129155 place¦129155.
