\v 15 \add ≈On¦129169 the previous day¦129164,\add* Yahweh¦129158 \add ≈had¦129159 quietly told\add* Shemuel¦129163,
\v 16 “About¦129172 this time¦129172 tomorrow¦129174, I'll¦129175 send¦129175 a Benyamite man¦129177 to you, and¦129180 you should anoint¦129180 him¦129180 to be ruler¦129181 over¦129182 my people Yisrael¦129185. He¦129186 will¦129186 \add ≈rescue¦129186\add* my people from¦129190 the Philistines¦129191, because I've¦129193 \add ≈noticed\add* my people because \add ≈I heard their¦129199 cries¦129199\add*.”
\p
\v 17 Then¦129202 Shemuel saw¦129203 Sha'ul¦129206, and¦129207 Yahweh¦129207 told him¦129208, “Look, \add that's\add* the¦129210 man¦129210 that I you¦129213 \add about\add*. \add ≈He¦129215\add* will¦129215 \add help control\add* my¦129216 people¦129216.”
