\p
\v 19 “I am¦129243 the seer¦129243,” Shemuel¦129237 answered¦129236, “\add Now,\add* Go¦129244 up¦129244 to the high¦129246 place¦129246 \add ≈ahead of me\add*, and¦129236 you'll eat¦129247 with¦129251 me today. In the morning¦129251, I'll tell¦129255 you \add ≈what you want to know\add*, then¦129236 I'll send¦129250 you off.
\v 20 As for¦129260 your donkeys¦129258 that¦129259 were¦129259 lost¦129259 three¦129262 days¦129263 ago, don't¦129264 \add ≈worry anymore about them¦129270\add* because¦129271 they've¦129272 been¦129272 found¦129272. Now, all¦129280 of Yisrael¦129277 is wanting your father's¦129282 \add ≈household¦129281\add*, and¦129258 \add ≡wanting\add* you \add in particular\add*.”
\v 21 “\add ≈But¦129285\add* I'm a Benyamite,” Sha'ul¦129286 responded¦129285, “\add That's\add* the smallest¦129293 tribe in Yisrael¦129296, and¦129297 my¦129297 clan's¦129297 the lowliest¦129298 of all¦129299 the Benyamite clans¦129301. \add ≈So\add* why \add ≈did you¦129305 talk to¦129306 me¦129306 like that¦129308\add*?”
\p
\v 22 Then Shemuel took¦129311 Sha'ul¦129315 and his¦129318 servant¦129318 to¦129320 the room¦129323 \add where the meal had been prepared\add*, and he¦129321 gave¦129321 them¦129322 a place¦129323 at¦129324 the head¦129324 of¦129324 \add ≈table—even above the invited¦129325 guests\add*. (There were about¦129327 thirty¦129327 men.)
\v 23 And Shemuel¦129331 told the cook¦129332, “Give¦129333 the \add special\add* \add ≈piece of meat\add* that¦129337 I \add ≈showed\add* you and¦129330 said¦129341 to keep aside.”
\v 24 \add ≈So¦129347\add* the cook¦129348 lifted¦129347 the \add ≈cooked leg\add* and¦129347 \add ≈placed it in¦129355 front¦129355\add* of¦129355 Sha'ul. Then¦129347 \add &Shemuel¦129377\add* told \add Sha'ul\add*, “Look, \add ≈this has¦129372 been reserved for you\add*. Eat¦129363 \add <it\add*, because¦129364 it's¦129366 been kept¦129366 \add ≈until\add* the appointed¦129365 time¦129365 \add ≈when I could call these people¦129370 together\add*.”
\s1 Shemuel anoints Sha'ul with oil
