\p
\v 1 Then Shemuel¦129439 took¦129438 a flask¦129442 of oil¦129443, and poured¦129444 it on¦129445 \add @Sha'ul's\add* head¦129447 and kissed¦129448 him, and told him, “It's¦129449 Yahweh¦129454 who has¦129453 anointed¦129453 you¦129453 to¦129458 be ruler¦129458 over¦129455 his¦129457 \add ≈chosen people\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈After you leave me¦129462 today\add* \add and get back to\add* Benyamite territory¦129470, then you'll \add ≈see\add* two¦129464 men¦129465 near¦129466 Rachel's¦129469 tomb in¦129470 Tseltsah, and they'll say¦129473 to you, ‘The¦129476 donkeys that¦129477 you went¦129478 to look for have¦129475 been found¦129475. \add ≈But¦129463\add*, wow, your¦129482 father¦129482 has¦129481 stopped worrying¦129487 about the donkeys and \add now\add* he's worried about \em you\em* \add ≈and trying to figure out what¦129490 he should do¦129491\add*.’
\v 3 Then¦129494 further¦129496 on¦129494 from¦129495 there¦129495, \add ≈as you approach\add* the¦129500 oak tree¦129500 at Tabor¦129501, you'll find¦129502 three men¦129505 going¦129506 to Beyt-El to worship God¦129509. One¦129510 will be taking three young goats, one will be carrying three rounds¦129521 loaves¦129521 of bread¦129522, and¦129494 one will be carrying a wine¦129527 in a container.
\v 4 They'll ask¦129529 about \add ≈how you're doing\add* and¦129529 give¦129532 you two¦129534 loaves of bread¦129536 which you should accept¦129537.
\v 5 After¦129540 that, you'll come¦129542 to the hill of God¦129544 (where¦129545 there's¦129547 a camp of Philistine \add warriors\add*). \add ≈When you enter\add* the town¦129553, you'll meet¦129554 a group of prophets¦129556 descending from¦129558 the \add ≈altar area\add*,
\v 6 and Yahweh's¦129570 spirit¦129569 will rush¦129567 onto you. Then¦129567 you'll \add join\add* them¦129572 in prophesying¦129571, and you'll be¦129573 transformed into¦129574 a different person¦129574.
\v 7 \add ≈When¦129577 this all comes¦129579 true\add*, do¦129584 whatever you think is correct because¦129578 God¦129590 \add ≈will be helping\add* you.
\v 8 Then¦129593 go¦129593 \add ≈ahead of me\add* to Gilgal¦129595 and wait \add there\add* for¦129594 seven¦129605 days¦129606, until¦129608 I get there and tell you what to do¦129616. I'll¦129612 join you to offer¦129600 burnt¦129601 offerings \add and\add* to sacrifice¦129602 peace¦129604 offerings.
\rem /s1 Saul Prophesies; Saul Made King; Samuel's Signs Are Fulfilled
\p
\v 9 Then as¦129619 Sha'ul \add ≈started to leave\add* Shemuel, God¦129627 \add ≈changed¦129624 his thinking\add*. Then all¦129631 Shemuel's predictions came¦129630 true that¦129636 day¦129635,
