\p
\v 12 \f + \fr 17:12 \ft Verses 12–31 aren't included in every ancient Greek translation.\f*\add ≈Now\add* David¦133598 was the son¦133599 of Yishay¦133608 (from the Efrat clan, he lived in Bethlehem in Yehudah¦133606) who had¦133616 eight¦133610 sons¦133611, and by Sha'ul's time¦133613, was quite old¦133615 compared to other men¦133617.\f + \fr 17:12 \ft There's a small variation in the original manuscripts at the end of the verse, but it has minimal effect on the essential story-line.\f*
\v 13 Yishay's¦133623 three¦133620 oldest sons¦133621 (Eliab¦133637, Abinadab¦133640, and¦133619 Shammah¦133642) had¦133625 gone¦133625 to¦133629 the¦133632 battle¦133636 with¦133636 Sha'ul¦133628,
