\p
\v 29 “What¦133936 have¦133937 I done¦133937 now¦133938?” David¦133935 \add ≈asked\add*. “Wasn't it¦133941 \add ≈just a question\add*?”
\v 30 Then¦133943 he¦133943 went over to¦133945 another¦133948 \add group\add* and \add ≈asked the same question and got the same answer¦133955\add*.
\p
\v 31 \add ≈So¦133958 it got around what David¦133963 was saying, and¦133958 when Sha'ul¦133967 heard¦133958 about it\add*, he sent¦133968 for¦133968 him¦133968.\f + \fr 17:31 \ft Verses 12–31 aren't included in every ancient Greek translation.\f*
