\v 32 David¦133971 told \add *the¦133974 king¦133974\add*, “Don't¦133975 \add ≈be discouraged\add*. Your¦133974 servant¦133982 will go¦133983 and¦133984 fight¦133984 against this¦133988 Philistine¦133987.”
\p
\v 33 “You can't¦133995 go¦133997 against¦133998 this¦134001 Philistine¦134000 and¦133990 fight¦134002 him¦134003,” Sha'ul¦133991 told David¦133994. “You're \add still\add* a lad, but¦133990 he's been a \add ≈professional warrior since¦134011 he was young\add*.”
\p
\v 34 “Your¦134021 servant¦134021 has been¦134020 \add working\add* for¦134022 his¦134022 father¦134022 tending the flock,” David¦134015 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add Sometimes\add* a lion¦134025 or a bear¦134028 has come¦134024 and \add ≈taken\add* a sheep¦134030 from¦134031 the flock
\v 35 and I would go after¦134034 it and \add ≈beat it\add* and rescue¦134036 \add <the sheep\add* from¦134037 its¦134037 mouth¦134037. If it \add ≈went¦134033 to attack\add* me¦134039, then¦134033 I'd grasp it by the jaw and beat it and kill¦134043 it.
\v 36 Your¦134046 servant¦134053 has¦134052 \add ≈killed\add* both a lion¦134048 and a bear¦134051, and that¦134057 uncircumcised¦134056 Philistine¦134055 will \add ≈end up\add* \add just\add* like¦134058 them¦134059, because¦134060 he's¦134061 insulted the \add ≈army\add* of¦134062 the living¦134064 God¦134063.”
\v 37 Then \add *he\add* added, “Yahweh who¦134070 has saved me from the lion¦134073 and¦134074 from the bear¦134075, \em he\em* will¦134077 \add be the one to\add* save me from that¦134080 Philistine¦134079.”
\p “Go¦134087 \add then\add*, and Yahweh be with¦134090 you¦134090.” Sha'ul¦134083 \add ≈assented\add*.
\v 38 Then¦134092 Sha'ul¦134093 \add had\add* David¦134096 dressed in his \add own battle\add* attire, and¦134092 then¦134092 in body¦134106 armour¦134106 with a bronze¦134100 helmet¦134099.
\v 39 David¦134109 strapped¦134108 his sword¦134112 over \add ≈the top\add* and¦134108 then¦134108 tried¦134115 to walk because¦134117 he hadn't been trained \add in wearing it\add*. \add ≈But¦134108\add* \add *he\add* told Sha'ul¦134125, “I \add ≈couldn't walk in all that without practice\add*,” \add ≈so\add* he took¦134133 it \add all\add* off.
\v 40 Then¦134137 he¦134137 \add ≈picked up\add* his staff¦134138, and selected five¦134143 smooth¦134144 stones¦134146 from¦134148 the riverbed¦134150. He¦134152 placed them¦134152 in¦134153 the pouch¦134158 of his shepherd's¦134154 bag¦134153, and \add ≈picked up\add* his sling¦134159 and \add ≈headed towards\add* the Philistine¦134164 \add champion\add*.
\s1 David fronts up to Goliat
