\p
\v 41 Then¦134166 \add @Goliat¦134167\add* came¦134168 closer and¦134166 closer to¦134170 David¦134172, with his¦134176 shield-bearer¦134175 walking in front¦134176 of him¦134176.
\v 42 When¦134179 \add *he\add* looked¦134178 and¦134178 \add ≈realised¦134180\add* that David¦134183 was a reddish, good-looking lad, he despised¦134184 him¦134184
\v 43 and¦134195 \add ≈asked\add* \add *him\add*, “Are you coming¦134205 to¦134207 me¦134207 with¦134208 a stick¦134208 because you think I'm a dog¦134200?” Then¦134195 the¦134210 Philistine cursed¦134209 David¦134199 by¦134214 his¦134214 gods¦134214.
\v 44 “Come¦134217 \add ≈over here\add*,” \add *he¦134216\add* told David¦134220, “and let me¦134222 give¦134223 your¦134226 flesh¦134226 to¦134227 the \add ≈vultures and wild animals¦134229\add*.”
\p
\v 45 “You're coming to me¦134240 with¦134241 a sword¦134241 and spear¦134242 and dagger,” David¦134234 \add ≈shouted back\add*. “But¦134233 I'm coming to you in¦134241 the name¦134248 of commander¦134250 Yahweh¦134249, the god¦134251 of Yisrael's¦134253 \add ≈army¦134250\add* that you've¦134255 been taunting.
\v 46 Today, Yahweh¦134260 will \add ≈help me defeat you\add* and I'll knock you down¦134262 and cut off your¦134266 head¦134266. \add ≈What's more,\add* I'll give¦134268 the Philistine army¦134270 corpses¦134269 to the \add ≈vultures and wild animals¦134276\add* today, then \add ≈everyone\add* will know¦134278 that¦134258 there's¦134283 a god¦134284 in¦134261 Yisrael¦134285.
\v 47 \add ≈Everyone¦134300 here will learn\add* that¦134291 Yahweh¦134298 doesn't save¦134297 with¦134295 swords¦134295 or spears¦134296, because¦134292 \add *he's\add* in¦134295 charge of the battle¦134301 and¦134287 will \add ≈help us defeat\add* you¦134303 all.”
\p
\v 48 Then¦134306 as \add @Goliat\add* went¦134311 closer to meet David, David ran¦134317 quickly¦134315 towards \add *him\add* at the battle¦134318 line¦134318.
\v 49 \add *He¦134322\add* \add ≈slipped\add* his hand¦134326 into his bag¦134329 and took¦134330 out a single stone and slung¦134333 it towards the Philistine¦134337—striking¦134334 him on¦134343 the forehead. The¦134323 stone sank¦134341 into his forehead and he¦134344 collapsed forwards onto the ground¦134348,
\v 50 and \add so\add* David¦134351 defeated the Philistine with a sling¦134355 and a stone¦134356—knocking him down¦134357 and killing¦134361 him. Not¦134363 having a sword¦134362 with him,\x + \xo 17:50: \xt 2Sam 21:19.\x*
\v 51 David¦134369 ran¦134368 and stood¦134370 over the¦134373 Philistine¦134373—drawing¦134378 \add @Goliat's\add* sword¦134377 out¦134378 of¦134379 its¦134379 sheath¦134379 to¦134371 kill¦134380 him¦134380 and cut¦134381 off¦134381 his¦134386 head¦134386.\x + \xo 17:51: \xt 2Sam 21:19.\x*
