\v 4 Yonatan¦134560 took off the¦134563 cloak that¦134564 he¦134566 was wearing and gave¦134566 it¦134566 to¦134567 David¦134567, along with his armour¦134568, his sword¦134571 and bow¦134574, and even his belt¦134577.
\v 5 David¦134580 went¦134579 \add ≈on¦134581 missions\add* wherever¦134582 Sha'ul sent¦134583 him and \add always\add* succeeded. Sha'ul \add ≈put him in¦134581 charge of¦134589 the warriors¦134589\add*, and that pleased¦134591 all¦134593 the people¦134595, as well as Sha'ul's servants¦134598.
