\p
\v 6 When \add ≈they'd all\add* come back after killing¦134606 the Philistine¦134609, the women¦134611 from¦134612 the Israeli¦134614 cities¦134614 had come out to meet¦134619 King¦134621 Sha'ul¦134620 with singing¦134616 and dancing¦134618—playing tambourines¦134622 and \add ≈other instruments¦134624 with great happiness\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈However\add*, as they danced¦134628 they sang¦134626,\x + \xo 18:7: \xt 1Sam 21:11; 29:5.\x*
\q1 “Sha'ul¦134631 has¦134630 \add ≈killed\add* his¦134632 thousands¦134632,
