\v 25 he¦134938 \add ≈replied\add*, “\add ≈Pass this onto\add* David, ‘The¦134947 king \add ≈doesn't want an expensive\add* bride¦134948 price—only a hundred¦134950 Philistine foreskins¦134951 taken from the king's¦134955 enemies¦134954.’ ” \add ≈But¦134938\add* Sha'ul¦134939 was \add still wanting\add* the Philistines¦134952 \add to be the ones\add* \add ≈to kill\add* David.
\v 26 \add ≈Now¦134976 when\add* David¦134968 \add ≈heard this from\add* the servants¦134967, \add ≈he decided that he could indeed marry the king's¦134978 daughter within the time¦134981 period that had been given\add*,
\v 27 \add ≈so\add* he and his men \add ≈got ready\add* and went¦134985 and \add ≈killed¦134989\add* \em two¦134991\em* hundred¦134991 Philistine men. He¦134993 brought¦134993 them to the king¦134999 and \add ≈had them counted to fulfill the pledge\add*, and so Sha'ul¦135005 \add had to\add* give his daughter¦135009 Mikal to become¦135000 his wife.
\p
\v 28 \add ≈But¦135013 when\add* Sha'ul¦135014 \add ≈realised¦135013\add* that Yahweh¦135017 was¦135018 \add ≈helping\add* David¦135020, and¦135021 that his daughter¦135022 loved¦135025 him¦135025,
