\p
\v 11 Sha'ul¦135270 sent¦135269 messengers¦135271 to watch¦135276 David's¦135275 house¦135274 to \add ≈kill¦135277\add* him in¦135278 the morning¦135278, but¦135269 his wife¦135282 Mikal told¦135279 \add *him\add*, “If¦135284 you don't¦135286 \add do something to\add* save your¦135290 life¦135290 tonight, you'll be dead by tomorrow¦135292.”\x + \xo 19:11: \xt Psa 59 header.\x*
\v 12 \add ≈So¦135296\add* Mikal¦135297 lowered¦135296 David¦135300 out through¦135301 the¦135302 window¦135302, and he was able to slip out and take off.
\v 13 Then¦135307 \add *she¦135307\add* took¦135307 a household idol¦135311 and put¦135312 it in¦135322 the bed, putting a goats' hair¦135318 quilt¦135317 \add ≈where the head¦135320 should be\add* and covering¦135321 it with¦135322 the \add bed-\add*clothes.
\v 14 \add ≈When\add* Sha'ul¦135326 sent¦135325 messengers¦135327 to¦135328 \add ≈arrest\add* David¦135331, she¦135332 \add ≈told\add* \add <them\add*, “He's¦135334 sick¦135333.”
\v 15 Sha'ul¦135338 sent¦135337 the¦135341 messengers¦135341 \add back\add*, \add ≈telling\add* \add <them\add*, “Bring¦135347 him up to¦135350 me¦135350 \add ≈bed¦135349 and¦135337 all so I¦135345 can kill¦135351 him\add*.”
\v 16 \add ≈But¦135353\add* when the messengers¦135354 \add ≈returned\add*, look, it was a household idol¦135356 in the bed¦135359 with a goats' hair¦135361 quilt¦135360 as its¦135362 head¦135362.
