\p “He \add ≈told me that he'd kill¦135388 me\add*,” Michal¦135368 \add ≈answered\add* Sha'ul, “\add ≈if I didn't help him escape¦135376\add*.”
\rem /s1 David Joins Samuel in Ramah
\p
\v 18 \add After\add* David¦135390 had slipped away, he went to Shemuel¦135411 in Ramah¦135397 and told¦135398 him everything that¦135404 Sha'ul¦135408 had done¦135405 to him, then¦135390 \add ≈the two of them\add* went and stayed in Nayot.
\v 19 \add ≈But¦135416\add* Sha'ul¦135417 was told¦135416 that David¦135420 was in¦135421 Nayot¦135421 \add ≈near\add* Ramah¦135423,
\v 20 \add ≈so\add* \add *he¦135425\add* sent¦135425 messengers to¦135428 \add ≈capture\add* David¦135431. \add ≈When¦135425\add* they saw¦135432 a group of¦135435 prophets¦135436 prophesying¦135437 and Shemuel¦135438 standing¦135439 \add ≈as head\add* over¦135441 them¦135441, God's spirit¦135447 came onto Sha'ul's messengers and they also¦135450 prophesied¦135449.
