\v 9 “\add I've only got\add* Goliat's sword,” \add ≈replied\add* the priest. “\add From\add* the Philistine who you \add ≈killed\add* in the Elah valley. Look, it's¦136624 wrapped in the cloak behind the sacred apron. If you want to¦136626 take it for yourself, take \add <it\add*, because¦136638 there's¦136628 no other \add ≈sword around\add* here.”
\p “\add Yes,\add* there's no \add ≈other sword\add* like it,” said¦136624 David¦136625. “\add ≈Get it for\add* me.”\x + \xo 21:9: \xt 1Sam 17:51.\x*
