\p
\v 11 Then¦137046 the king \add ≈summoned\add* Ahitub's¦137054 son¦137052 Ahimelek¦137051 and all his¦137060 relatives who¦137062 were¦137063 priests¦137055 to Nob¦137063, and they¦137064 all came¦137064 to the king.
\v 12 “Listen¦137073 now, son¦137076 of¦137076 Ahitub¦137078,” said¦137079 Sha'ul¦137072.
\p “\add ≈Go ahead\add* my¦137081 master¦137081,” \add ≈answered\add* Ahimelek.
\p
\v 13 “Why have¦137088 you all conspired¦137088 against me?” asked Sha'ul¦137086. “You gave¦137094 bread¦137097 to¦137096 Yishay's¦137093 son¦137091, and a sword¦137098, and you \add ≈asked guidance from\add* God¦137101 for him¦137084, \add so now\add* he's risen up¦137102 against me—lying in¦137094 ambush¦137104 this¦137106 very day¦137105?”
\p
\v 14 “\add ≈Isn't David¦137119 one of your most\add* faithful¦137120 servants¦137118?” Ahimelek answered¦137109 the king. “He's the king's¦137122 son-in-law¦137121 and commander over your guards, and isn't he honoured¦137127 in your house¦137128?
\v 15 Did¦137131 I begin¦137131 to inquire¦137132 for¦137138 him¦137141 from God¦137136 today? Far¦137137 be¦137137 it¦137137 from me¦137138! Don't¦137139 let¦137141 the¦137142 king¦137142 \add ≈accuse\add* his servant or any of my father's¦137148 household¦137147, because¦137149 your¦137153 servant doesn't know¦137152 about any of this—\add ≈nothing at¦137136 all¦137154\add*.”
