\v 4 David's¦137928 men¦137929 \add ≈whispered\add* to him, “Wow, today what Yahweh told you \add ≈is coming¦137912 true\add* \add when he said\add*, ‘Listen, I'm about to give \add ≈victory over your enemy\add*, and you will do to him \add ≈whatever you think is right\add*.’ ” Then David \add ≈sneaked up\add* and \add ≈quietly\add* cut \add a piece\add* off the¦137930 edge of¦137930 Sha'ul's robe.
\v 5 \add ≈Afterwards\add* \add however,\add* David¦137937 \add ≈felt bad because\add* he'd cut¦137961 \add a piece\add* off¦137961 Sha'ul's \add ≈clothes\add*
\v 6 and¦137973 he said to his men, “\add ≈By Yahweh, I shouldn't have¦137984 done that¦137988\add* to my master—to Yahweh's anointed \add king\add*—to \add ≈do him¦137981 harm\add* because he's¦137984 the¦137987 \add one\add* Yahweh anointed.”\x + \xo 24:6: \xt 1Sam 26:11.\x*
\v 7 \add *He¦137993\add* restrained his¦137994 men¦137994 with \add a few quiet\add* words and¦137993 \add ≈wouldn't allow them to attack\add* Sha'ul.
\p Then Sha'ul left the cave and \add ≈headed down the path\add*.
\v 8 After \add ≈waiting a few moment\add*, David went¦138033 out of¦138022 the cave¦138032 and called out behind Sha'ul, “My master the king.” \add ≈When\add* Sha'ul turned and looked behind him, David bowed
\v 9 and said, “Why do you listen to \add ≈people when they say¦138052 that I'm wanting to harm you\add*?
\v 10 Look, \add ≈you can see for yourself\add* that Yahweh gave \add ≈me the opportunity to harm\add* you today in the cave, and some \add of my men\add* wanted me to kill you, but¦138066 I \add ≈showed you\add* compassion and \add ≈told them that\add* I wouldn't \add ≈do¦138070 harm to\add* my master, because he's Yahweh's \add ≈chosen king\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈Your majesty, look¦138099 of this piece of your¦138086 robe that I'm holding\add*, because¦138107 when I cut it¦138099 off, I didn't¦138102 kill you. \add ≈So now you can see¦138085 for yourself that I have¦138085 no evil plans, and I haven't do you any wrong, even though\add* you're \add ≈ambushing me so you can kill me\add*.
