\p
\v 16 \add ≈When David finished saying that to Sha'ul, Sha'ul called back\add*, “Is that your voice, my¦138205 son David?” Then \add *he¦138206\add* \add ≈cried loudly\add*
\v 17 and¦138211 told David¦138214, “You're more righteous than I \add am\add*, because you \add ≈were\add* good to me \add ≈even when I\add* did evil \add things\add* to you.
\v 18 You've \add ≈stated\add* that you've¦138244 \add ≈treated me well\add*—how Yahweh \add ≈gave you the advantage over me, yet\add* you didn't kill me.
\v 19 \add ≈Now\add* if a man finds his enemy \add unprepared\add*, does¦138258 he¦138263 \add just\add* \add ≈send him off happily\add*? \add ≈Well,\add* may Yahweh¦138264 reward you¦138267 for \add ≈your¦138265 mercy towards\add* me¦138267 today.
