\v 7 Now I've¦138446 heard¦138446 those shearers¦138448 \add ≈are working for\add* you, and¦138459 your shepherds¦138451 have¦138455 been \add ≈living\add* with¦138468 us¦138456. We¦138458 haven't harmed them or \add ≈taken anything¦138463 of theirs¦138467\add* while they've been in¦138468 Carmel¦138468.
\v 8 Ask your \add ≈servants\add* and they'll \add ≈confirm this\add*. May \add these\add* young¦138477 men¦138477 \add ≈enjoy your\add* favour¦138478 because¦138480 \add harvesting the wool\add* is a \add ≈prosperous time\add*, so I request a gift for your servants and for your ‘son¦138495’, David¦138496.’ ”
