\v 9 \add ≈So¦138498\add* David's¦138500 men¦138499 went¦138498 and \add ≈passed all¦138505 that onto\add* Nabal¦138504, and then¦138498 \add ≈waited¦138511 for his response\add*.
\v 10 \add ≈But¦138513\add* Nabal¦138514 answered¦138513 \add *them\add*, “\add ≈Why should I care about\add* David¦138518? Yishay's¦138525 son¦138523 \add ≈isn't anyone¦138530 important\add*. There's lot of¦138517 servants¦138528 \add ≈these days\add* who are \add ≈on the run from¦138531 their¦138532\add* \add #masters¦138532\add*.
